  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding of Alaska Medicaid Kesimpta (ofatumumab), a CD20-directed cytolytic antibody. Version: 1; Original: 12/05/20; Approval: 1/15/21; Effective: 3/15/21.",
    "Encoded: three closed adult relapsing MS indications, approval criteria 1-7 and denial criteria 2-3. Denial criterion 1 (failure to meet approval criteria) is covered by the approval clauses. Monitoring, vaccination windows, screening and prior therapy are attestations.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval up to 3 months; reauthorization approval up to 12 months.",
    "Quantity (notes only): 4 injections for the initial month load dosing; 1 injection every 4 weeks for maintenance dosing. No numeric quantity enforcement.",
    "Cautions (notes only): patients of reproductive potential should use effective contraception due to possible fetal risks. Consider discontinuing Kesimpta for serious opportunistic infection or recurrent infections if immunoglobulin levels indicate immune compromise. Treat injection site reactions based on severity.",
    "PDL status unknown: PDF is silent. Briumvi is an encoded CD20 MS peer; alternative eligibility requires separate evaluation.",
    "Remaining gaps: documentation verification, authorization duration, reauthorization, dosing, quantity enforcement and cautions require manual review."
  ],
